<p>A fire at Viva Energy’s Geelong refinery in Corio, near Melbourne, broke out just after 11pm on Wednesday and burned for about 13 hours before firefighters extinguished it on Thursday. Authorities said the blaze was concentrated in the motor gasoline section of one of Australia’s two operating refineries, with flames reported as high as 60 metres. No injuries were reported, and hazardous materials teams said monitoring had not detected contaminants around the site. The fire has raised concerns about short-term petrol supply and prices because the Geelong refinery supplies about half of Victoria’s fuel and around 10% of Australia’s fuel, while the damaged section is linked to high-octane petrol production. Officials said diesel and jet fuel units were protected after isolation valves were triggered, while damage assessments continue and replacement petrol imports are being arranged.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oP0c9Q6pNfxRRokK5rNgcdvoiU7uZYRGnCpkTvxZG0N0w6l2AHiBXZqrgI4pGeIjfeP8ZZLQO8dMVP_q7F9gKDZUL47pY3ZvRsKKxv1Gku5J' alt='Aerial view of the Viva Oil Refinery in Geelong after the overnight fire on April 16, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Fire response: About 50 firefighting vehicles stayed on scene as crews worked overnight, and officials said the fire began to ease as refinery systems and pipework depressurised.</li><li>Price risk: Experts told The Guardian that Victorian fuel prices could rise by up to 20 Australian cents a litre, and some petrol stations could face brief outages, though national supply is not expected to be hit.</li><li>Possible trigger: Firefighters said flames erupted after a gas leak ignited late on Wednesday, after what authorities described as a chain of explosions at the refinery.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Fire Rescue Victoria: Assistant chief fire officer Mick McGuinness said the blaze was still not under control early Thursday and was being fed mainly by liquid petrol, gas and vapours, which is why crews quickly warned the community about smoke. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/apr/16/anthony-albanese-brunei-visit-fuel-crisis-labor-richard-marles-coalition-immigration-plan-angus-taylor-employment-figures-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Energy Minister Chris Bowen: Bowen said the refinery fire was &quot;not a positive development&quot; at a time when Australia’s fuel supplies were already under pressure from conflict in the Middle East. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992249/fuel-supply-fears-after-blaze-tears-through-crucial-australian-refinery'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Supply chain experts: Specialists told The Guardian that the outage was more likely to cause a sharp but regional disruption in Victoria than a nationwide fuel crunch, because replacement supply can be redirected. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/16/victoria-fuel-prices-geelong-viva-oil-refinery-fire'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/firefighters-battle-huge-blaze-at-australian-oil-refinery/a-76801562'>Firefighters battle huge blaze at Australian oil refinery</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/apr/16/anthony-albanese-brunei-visit-fuel-crisis-labor-richard-marles-coalition-immigration-plan-angus-taylor-employment-figures-ntwnfb'>News live: Australia secures 100m litres of diesel from Brunei and South Korea; Paul Keating lashes Liberals’ immigration policy</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/australasia/article/3350236/fire-australian-refinery-fuels-petrol-shortage-fears-amid-global-oil-crisis'>Fire at Australian refinery fuels petrol shortage fears amid global oil crisis</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992249/fuel-supply-fears-after-blaze-tears-through-crucial-australian-refinery'>Fuel supply fears after blaze tears through crucial Australian refinery</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='